  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "molecular-accelerating-3fc4",
  "summary": "HiFi, Hi-C and multi-genome de novo assemblies now resolve sex chromosome turnover and centromeric and segmental duplication content in non-model taxa.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of multiple or sex-specific de novo assemblies to resolve structurally complex regions in non-model taxa, with sex chromosomes as the focal case. The degu preprint combines HiFi and Hi-C data to achieve chromosome-level contiguity and reports centromere and segmental duplication annotation. The mountain pine beetle preprint assembles six new genomes to reconstruct stepwise neo-Y formation and reports rapid, population-specific neo-Y degeneration. The published Onthophagus binodis study delivers sex-specific chromosome-level assemblies, using a hybrid reference and repeat expansion analysis to examine putative Y chromosome content. What is new relative to the human-centric resolution work is the emphasis on comparative and population-level sampling of sex chromosome turnover, with assembly multiplicity itself serving as the analytical tool.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-31"
}
